.TH ORO-MIGRATION 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:migration \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:migration'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Bundled historical protected imports and retained Android component handover. Aliases, codecs, AAD and component identities come from immutable project data. Original records/keys and uncertain receipts are preserved. Account authority, historical schema and authenticated server reconciliation remain application policy.
.PP
Platform support: Android only, with `[migration] enabled = true`, bundled definitions and an SDK reporting historicalMigrationProtocol 1. Protected imports require Android 11+ authentication\-bound keys. iOS/iPadOS, macOS, Linux and Windows historical migration backends are not implemented. `getSupport()` reports unavailable with a platform/reason; operational calls reject ENOSYS. There is no fallback to plaintext storage or background JS. Source implementation and a support probe do not establish historical signed upgrade, production signing, OEM authentication or server reconciliation acceptance. Fixed `prefer\-native\-records\-v1` source selection uses legacy ciphertext only while the native scope is absent. A present scope is authoritative; missing rows, lost keys and provenance mismatches never fall back to legacy data. `[migration] generate_adapters = false` bundles identical policy for a bridge build retaining existing app components. Generated adapters do not continue old alarm presentation before an explicitly approved replacement handover.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBgetSupport()\fR
Probe without prompting, creating keys or reading legacy values. Other platforms and older runtimes report unavailable; operational calls still reject ENOSYS. Android implements this backend. iOS/iPadOS, macOS, Linux and Windows return reason migration\-backend\-unimplemented; older Android SDKs return migration\-protocol\-unavailable. A configured backend can be unavailable due to disabled/malformed bundled definitions; inspect error before enabling UI.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<MigrationSupport>\fR
.TP
\fBinspectProtected(options)\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ProtectedSource; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ProtectedSourceStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBimportProtected(options, settings)\fR
Opens the bundled historical envelope with its original key, then rewraps to an authentication\-bound runtime key. Each protected cryptographic operation uses its own system prompt. No plaintext is returned. The original source digest is rechecked before commit; retry/discovery recovers an already committed import. After explicit user recovery, a fresh recoveryRef rewraps the still\-readable original into a new key/handle while preserving earlier imports. Reuse that recoveryRef to reconcile a lost reply. Missing original keys are never replaced.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ProtectedImportOptions; required)
.br
\fIsettings\fR (MigrationRequestOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ProtectedImport>\fR
.TP
\fBopenProtected(options, settings)\fR
Unlock a migrated value for the owning private interactive form. This always uses the new key's per\-operation prompt, never a cached authentication boolean.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ProtectedOpenOptions; required)
.br
\fIsettings\fR (MigrationRequestOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ProtectedValue>\fR
.TP
\fBdiscoverProtected(options)\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ProtectedIdentity; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ProtectedImport[]>\fR
.TP
\fBreadUnprotected(options, settings)\fR
Read only a bundled noninteractive source explicitly marked exposure: private\-document. Requires native foreground consent and returns Base64 to that private document. Authentication\-bound sources always reject this path. Never expose the result through logs, assistant tools or background handlers.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (UnprotectedReadOptions; required)
.br
\fIsettings\fR (MigrationRequestOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<UnprotectedValue>\fR
.TP
\fBgetHistoricalEntries(options)\fR
Read bounded opaque references captured from an allowlisted historical Activity action. Primary window only. Every entry is untrusted: authorize its destination in the current account before navigating or performing work.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HistoricalEntryOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<HistoricalEntry[]>\fR
.TP
\fBacknowledgeHistoricalEntry(options)\fR
Acknowledge an owned routing entry after application validation. This does not acknowledge a source alarm, remote operation or notification delivery.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HistoricalEntryId; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<HistoricalEntryAcknowledgement>\fR
.TP
\fBinspectHandover(options)\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HistoricalComponentSource; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<HistoricalSourceStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBprepareHandover(options, settings)\fR
Prepare an exact source/replacement binding after native consent. Pass an empty expectedGeneration only for an absent mapping. Bundled identity fields must match the already\-authorized workflow binding; no server authority is inferred.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HandoverOptions; required)
.br
\fIsettings\fR (MigrationRequestOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<HandoverStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBdiscoverHandovers(options)\fR
Rediscover exact owned generations after an interrupted reply, including Stop. An existing historical reference cannot be rebound to another account/authority.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HandoverIdentity; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DiscoveredHandover[]>\fR
.TP
\fBactivateHandover(options)\fR
Activate only the prepared generation after rechecking source and replacement. The original component names, job IDs/schedules and encrypted receipts remain. This neither unregisters old endpoints nor claims remote migration completion.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HandoverId; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<HandoverStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBgetHandoverStatus(options)\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HandoverId; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<HandoverStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBstopHandover(options)\fR
Fence this generation and cancel its admitted reads. Poll drained before treating owned cleanup as complete. Already\-submitted effects stay uncertain.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HandoverId; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<HandoverStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBgetRetainedReceipts(options)\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (HandoverId; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<RetainedReceipt[]>\fR
.TP
\fBresolveRetainedReceipt(options)\fR
Record an application\-verified result without claiming runtime verification of its server. Repeated identical resolutions are idempotent; changed ones conflict.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ReceiptResolution; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ReceiptResolutionResult>\fR
.TP
\fBreleaseRetainedReceipt(options)\fR
Release only an explicitly resolved receipt. Unknown receipts never expire or disappear automatically; at capacity new admission returns ENOSPC.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (RetainedReceiptId; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ReceiptReleaseResult>\fR
